{"calculus_ref":"stdo://releases/v2.5.1-rc.2/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md","clause_relations":[{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:applicability","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:reference-frame","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"A frame name, an available tool or a listed family triggers no activation by itself. Where applicability needs residual semantic judgment, that judgment and its evidence are retained as a judgment, never represented as a computed fact.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6, P1","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:a-name-tool-or-family-triggers-no-activation"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:coverage-ledger","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:evaluation-inventory","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Artifact presence, file count, operation count, test count or repository reachability proves no evaluation coverage.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:artifact-presence-proves-no-coverage"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:coverage-ledger","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:semantic-authority","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:decision-authority","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:operation-authority","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Every material evaluation identifies semantic and decision authority. Every material operation also identifies its existing construction, transformation, admission, publication or mutation authority. A frame set with broad observational reach, an unresolved decision owner or an effectful path without operation authority is not closed.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:authority-coverage-closes-only-with-owners-named"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:invalidator","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:closed-result","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Changed material inputs or a declared revising observation invalidate the affected result before reliance, preserving its predecessor/successor relation and any demonstrably independent surviving results; a changed basis invalidates likewise.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:counterevidence-invalidates-dependents","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"literal":"Return A Closed Result names inputs and observation; TICKET judgment continuity names basis.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:changed-inputs-invalidate-before-reliance"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:result-algebra","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:coverage","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"A composite over several results declares its conjunction; the member it reports is chosen by that declared rule; every known failure and uncovered obligation survives the join and is carried with the composite; no universal order among the non-satisfied members exists.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:failure-and-uncovered-obligation-survive-join","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:composite-reports-by-declared-conjunction"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:claim","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Later counterevidence arrives.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:condition"},{"literal":"Every dependent verdict is invalidated until the claim-evidence relation is superseded, withdrawn or requalified.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:consequence"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:counterevidence-invalidates-dependents"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:coverage-tuple","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:coverage-ledger","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Coverage is evaluated against the tuple Coverage(W, G, B, E, S, T): the workspace W, the governed outcome G, the exact basis B, the known evaluation inventory E, the declared frame set S and the time or immutable checkpoint T of the claim. Changing any material member may invalidate the coverage result.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P3, P6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:coverage-is-relative-to-its-tuple"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:coverage-ledger","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"The ledger holds at least, for each evaluation: evaluation (the exact question or predicate); provenance (the source establishing materiality); subject and basis (the exact workspace coordinate); selected frames (the frames capable of evaluating it); actor envelope (the competence and context required); semantic authority (the owner of the evaluated meaning); operation authority (the existing owner grant where the evaluation performs a construction, transformation, admission, publication or mutation; otherwise none); decision authority (the owner of the disposition); evidence (the required observations and their provenance); dependencies (material frame or seam relations); status (the coverage disposition); residual (uncertainty, exclusion or re-entry condition).","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P4b, P6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:coverage-ledger-fields"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:coverage-status","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:coverage-ledger","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"The baseline coverage statuses are covered, separately_covered, conditionally_covered, conflicted, uncovered, unknown and excluded_by_authority.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P4b, P6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:coverage-statuses-are-seven"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:completeness-boundary","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:coverage-ledger","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Coverage stays falsifiable and externally challengeable. Challenge sources include human knowledge outside the current frame set; independent review; historical failures and predecessor systems; mutation, adversarial and counterexample search; live operation and user behaviour; adjacent workspace or domain comparison; and changes in actor capability, law, dependencies or topology. The method requires an explicit residual boundary and never a claim of metaphysical or universal completeness.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"RF-015","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:coverage-stays-falsifiable-and-challengeable"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:decision-rule","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:result-conjunction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"A declared decision rule consumes closed frame results. The rule states which results are mandatory; how conflict and indeterminacy are handled; which basis relations must agree; which decision authority owns the conjunction; and whether any result may veto or defer the decision.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6, P4a","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:composite-reports-by-declared-conjunction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:decision-rule-states-its-terms"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:diagnostic-order","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Diagnosis asks, in this order: 1 Was the correct declared frame activated? 2 Were the subject and basis exact? 3 Was the actor inside the capability envelope? 4 Was admissible evidence available? 5 Is a material variable or invariant missing from the frame? 6 Is a required conjunction or translation missing? 7 Is the evaluation family itself wrong or incomplete? 8 Is another frame required? The order prevents every difficult evaluation from creating another frame.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P2","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:diagnostic-order-is-eight-questions-in-order"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:coverage","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"A composite with a known failure or an uncovered required obligation cannot project success; a known failure A and an uncovered obligation B survive every join.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:uncovered-coverage-is-r-minus-c","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:failure-and-uncovered-obligation-survive-join"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:frame-set-declaration","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:frame-set-authority","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Human authority may declare an initial project frame set from accumulated practice, known failure modes, domain expertise, the outcome's risk and knowledge of the available actors, without reconstructing it from the workspace bottom up. The declaration records: the governed workspace and outcome; the known evaluation inventory; the selected frames and their capability envelopes; intentional overlaps and separately activated checks; known frame dependencies or translations; semantic, evaluation, operation where material, decision and acceptance authority; known exclusions and residual uncertainty; and the conditions for revision.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P6, P2","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:frame-set-declaration-records-its-fields"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:evaluation-inventory","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"The coverage evaluator derives the known evaluation inventory from every material available source, including where applicable: goals, intent, product definition, requirements and accepted method; accepted design, its ontology, identities, lifecycles, authorities and algorithms; implementation capabilities and externally observable behaviour; operational, release, security, safety and governance obligations; dependencies and interaction seams; evidence, tests, scenarios, qualification and acceptance claims; historical tickets, check-ins, commentary, post-mortems, incidents and rejected candidates; days-long loops, resets, repeated repairs and discovered rival paths; known agent capability limits and prior invisible violations; and applicable external law, contracts or standards. The inventory records provenance and materiality.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P2, P6","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:inventory-is-derived-from-every-material-source-with-provenance"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:result-conjunction","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:coverage-status","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Every mandatory constraint is satisfied with valid applicable evidence. Common agreement cannot discard a constraint or a material counterexample that only one contributor found. A missing, wrong-subject, conflicted or indeterminate mandatory result stays unresolved under the declared rule; aggregate green status cannot replace it.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P4b, P5","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:failure-and-uncovered-obligation-survive-join","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:forbids","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:mandatory-unresolved-result-survives-aggregate-green"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:revision-action","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:frame-set","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Every material revision changes frame identity or revision coordinates and states which prior activations, results and coverage claims require reevaluation.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P3, P4b","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:changed-inputs-invalidate-before-reliance","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:material-revision-changes-identity-and-names-reevaluation"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:missing-frame-signal","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:diagnostic-order","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"These observations trigger frame diagnosis: a competent actor repeatedly cannot see a known material violation; a local repair creates or duplicates another authority path; work repeatedly resets after apparently valid local completion; long implementation loops produce no stable closure; proof passes while the claimed outcome stays unbound; a material failure is visible only after broad integration; reviewers repeatedly expand context without reaching a decidable question; two actors use the same frame name but evaluate different material relations; or a topology mutation leaves prior verdicts apparently current.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P4b, P5","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:missing-frame-signals-enumerated"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:diagnostic-order","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:evaluation-family","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:rf-001-evaluation-relativity","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:target"},{"literal":"Question 1 is answered by family inclusion, not by set membership. An evaluation is within a frame's family when the question it decides is one the frame's declared evaluation family states, at the frame's declared coordinates. Membership of the frame in the frame set, the frame's name, a role label or similar wording of the question does not place an evaluation in the frame's family; an activation of a frame on an evaluation outside its family answers question 1 no, whatever the frame's standing in the set.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P2, P1; RF-001; the material relation drawn is evaluation-to-family inclusion; rc.2 #diagnostic-order, #evaluation, #rf-001-evaluation-relativity, #applicability-and-required-results","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:a-name-tool-or-family-triggers-no-activation","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:diagnostic-order-is-eight-questions-in-order","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:rf-001-every-frame-declares-its-evaluation-family","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:question-one-is-answered-by-family-inclusion"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:revision-action","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:function-revise","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"A revision may: clarify activation or evidence acquisition; change the capability envelope; add or remove a material relation; split an overloaded frame; merge duplicative frames where capability and authority stay sound; add intentional overlap; add or revise a conjunction or translation; retire a frame whose evaluation family is no longer material; or revise the project evaluation inventory.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P4b","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:revision-actions-enumerated"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:revision-action","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:closed-result","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:coordinate","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"Stated plainly: a material revision of a frame produces a new frame revision coordinate. Every prior closed result bound to the previous revision of a materially revised frame is bound to a mismatched coordinate (RF-005) and is invalidated for reuse until it is re-checked against the new revision. The revision record lists those results as reopened; a result leaves that list only by a recorded re-check that finds it demonstrably independent of the change, or by re-evaluation on the new revision. A material revision does not select which of the results bound to the prior revision it reopens, and silence does not keep a result closed. A non-material revision, for example one that clarifies an activation or acquires evidence without changing any declaration, produces no new coordinate and reopens no result; the revision record states that the revision is non-material.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P3, P4b; RF-005, RF-011, ACTIVATION section 7; rc.2 #revision-actions, #rf-005-exact-basis-and-coordinates, #return-a-closed-result","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:changed-inputs-invalidate-before-reliance","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:material-revision-changes-identity-and-names-reevaluation","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:rf-005-every-result-binds-exact-basis-and-coordinates","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:rf-011-topology-mutation-forces-reevaluation-before-reuse","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:revision-reopens-every-result-bound-to-the-prior-revision"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:reference-frame","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:evaluation-family","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:rf-001-evaluation-relativity","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:target"},{"literal":"Every frame declares the evaluation family it supports. A frame with no declared evaluation family has no testable sufficiency boundary.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P2","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:rf-001-every-frame-declares-its-evaluation-family"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:closed-result","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:basis","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:coordinate","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:rf-005-exact-basis-and-coordinates","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:target"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:r-invalid-basis","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:target"},{"literal":"Every result binds its exact subject, basis, coordinates and evidence scope. A stale, advanced, ambiguous or mismatched basis returns invalid_basis or requires reactivation. Apparent equality never substitutes for declared coordinate equality.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P3, P1","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:rf-005-every-result-binds-exact-basis-and-coordinates"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:activated-frame","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:topology","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:rf-011-topology-mutation-and-recharting","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:target"},{"literal":"An activated frame declares the topology changes capable of invalidating its coordinates or its materiality judgment. A detected material topology mutation causes reevaluation, frame revision or recharting before the previous result is reused. Material revision of the frame itself invalidates for reuse every result bound to the prior revision coordinate; §10 Revision actions states that rule.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"},{"literal":"P3, P4b","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:qualification"},{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:changed-inputs-invalidate-before-reliance","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:support"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:rf-011-topology-mutation-forces-reevaluation-before-reuse"},{"arguments":[{"ref":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:symbol:coverage","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:subject"},{"literal":"For required obligations R and admitted coverage C, uncovered coverage is R minus C; combining results takes the union of known failures and recomputes uncovered coverage.","role":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:role:requirement"}],"clause_type":"constraint","operator":"urn:stdo-3:claude:vocabulary:operator:requires","uri":"urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:uncovered-coverage-is-r-minus-c"}],"closure":{"clauses":["urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:a-name-tool-or-family-triggers-no-activation","urn:stdo-3:claude:a-c-text:clause:artifact-presence-proves-no-coverage","urn:stdo-3:claude:a